From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Nov 2026 07:10:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: return no picture for a frame the gen2 firmware
 does not show

For a frame that is decoded but not shown, such as a VP9 alt-ref frame
packed in a superframe, the gen2 firmware returns the output buffer with
HFI_PROP_PICTURE_TYPE NOSHOW and the length of a whole picture. iris
flagged the buffer V4L2_BUF_FLAG_ERROR but kept that length and the
timestamp. Chromium's stateful decoder outputs every CAPTURE buffer
whose bytesused is not zero and does not look at the error flag.

Return such a buffer with no payload and no timestamp, as the gen1 path
now does. Valve's startup_machine.webm, which the Steam client plays,
has 11 hidden frames in 94 packets: on a KONKR Pocket FIT Elite
(SM8750) ffmpeg got 105 pictures from it, all equal to frames that
software decoding shows.

Signed-off-by: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2_response.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2_response.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2_response.c
index f0782c4..8bbd2c3 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2_response.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2_response.c
@@ -390,6 +390,12 @@ static int iris_hfi_gen2_handle_output_buffer(struct iris_inst *inst,
 
 	buf->flags = iris_hfi_gen2_get_driver_buffer_flags(inst, hfi_buffer->flags);
 
+	/* A frame not to be shown (VP9 hidden frame): no picture, as on gen1 */
+	if (to_iris_inst_hfi_gen2(inst)->hfi_frame_info.picture_type & HFI_GEN2_PICTURE_NOSHOW) {
+		buf->data_size = 0;
+		buf->timestamp = 0;
+	}
+
 	if (!buf->data_size && inst->state == IRIS_INST_STREAMING &&
 	    !(hfi_buffer->flags & HFI_BUF_FW_FLAG_LAST)) {
 		buf->flags |= V4L2_BUF_FLAG_ERROR;
-- 
2.47.0

